      "text": "easily handle this by setting up two environments (like [www.yourdomain.com](https://www.yourdomain.com) for marketing and app.yourdomain.com for the whiteboard).\n\nHere is the exact production-level page structure you'll need to build:\n\n1. The Marketing Site (Public & SEO-Optimized)\nThis is your storefront. It needs to be fast, responsive, and designed to convert visitors into users.\n\n/ (Home/Landing Page): Hero section with a clear call-to-action (CTA), interactive preview gif/video of the whiteboard, social proof, and a footer.\n\n/features: Deep dive into realtime collaboration, team workspaces, and export options.\n\n/pricing: Clear breakdown of your Free, Premium, and Team tiers.\n\n/blog (Optional but good): For SEO and updates (you already have experience building a Corporate Blog!).\n\n/contact & /about: Standard trust-building pages.\n\n/legal/privacy & /legal/terms: Essential for any SaaS taking payments and storing user data.\n\n2. The Core Web App (Authenticated Area)\nThis is where the magic happens. It handles authentication, routing, state management, and the WebSocket connections for real-time drawing.\n\nAuthentication & Onboarding\n\n/login & /signup: Secure entry points.\n\n/onboarding: A quick flow for new users to name their first Team/Organization and invite their first members.\n\nThe Dashboard & Workspaces\n\n/dashboard: The main hub showing recently accessed boards, templates, and quick actions.\n\n/t/[teamId]: The specific view for an Organization/Team showing all boards belonging to that group.\n\n/t/[teamId]/members: The hub for invite-only collaboration. Here, admins can invite people via email, assign roles (Viewer, Editor, Admin), and manage access.\n\n/t/[teamId]/settings: Workspace preferences (name, logo, deletion).\n\nThe Whiteboard Engine\n\n/board/[boardId]: The absolute core of your app. This is the full-screen canvas UI (toolbar, canvas area, active users cursors).\n\nNote: The \"Public, View-Only\" links will also route here, but your frontend logic will check their permissions and hide the drawing toolbars if they are just a viewer.\n\nMonetization & User Settings\n\n/settings/profile: User avatar, name, and password management.\n\n/settings/billing: This page will connect to your payment gateway (like Stripe or Razorpay). It should show the current active plan, billing history, and a button to \"Manage Subscription\" or \"Upgrade\".",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "easily handle this by setting up two environments (like [www.yourdomain.com](https://www.yourdomain.com) for marketing and app.yourdomain.com for the whiteboard).\n\nHere is the exact production-level page structure you'll need to build:\n\n1. The Marketing Site (Public & SEO-Optimized)\nThis is your storefront. It needs to be fast, responsive, and designed to convert visitors into users.\n\n/ (Home/Landing Page): Hero section with a clear call-to-action (CTA), interactive preview gif/video of the whiteboard, social proof, and a footer.\n\n/features: Deep dive into realtime collaboration, team workspaces, and export options.\n\n/pricing: Clear breakdown of your Free, Premium, and Team tiers.\n\n/blog (Optional but good): For SEO and updates (you already have experience building a Corporate Blog!).\n\n/contact & /about: Standard trust-building pages.\n\n/legal/privacy & /legal/terms: Essential for any SaaS taking payments and storing user data.\n\n2. The Core Web App (Authenticated Area)\nThis is where the magic happens. It handles authentication, routing, state management, and the WebSocket connections for real-time drawing.\n\nAuthentication & Onboarding\n\n/login & /signup: Secure entry points.\n\n/onboarding: A quick flow for new users to name their first Team/Organization and invite their first members.\n\nThe Dashboard & Workspaces\n\n/dashboard: The main hub showing recently accessed boards, templates, and quick actions.\n\n/t/[teamId]: The specific view for an Organization/Team showing all boards belonging to that group.\n\n/t/[teamId]/members: The hub for invite-only collaboration. Here, admins can invite people via email, assign roles (Viewer, Editor, Admin), and manage access.\n\n/t/[teamId]/settings: Workspace preferences (name, logo, deletion).\n\nThe Whiteboard Engine\n\n/board/[boardId]: The absolute core of your app. This is the full-screen canvas UI (toolbar, canvas area, active users cursors).\n\nNote: The \"Public, View-Only\" links will also route here, but your frontend logic will check their permissions and hide the drawing toolbars if they are just a viewer.\n\nMonetization & User Settings\n\n/settings/profile: User avatar, name, and password management.\n\n/settings/billing: This page will connect to your payment gateway (like Stripe or Razorpay). It should show the current active plan, billing history, and a button to \"Manage Subscription\" or \"Upgrade\".",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
