      "text": "DONE ✅\n1. UI/UX Layout Strategy (BoardPage)\nFull-screen whiteboard with clean, distraction-free UI.\nCanvas covers entire screen (100vw × 100vh).\nTop navbar: board name, users, share & export buttons.\nLeft toolbar: pen, shapes, text, sticky notes, eraser.\nRight sidebar: edit properties or open AI tools.\nBottom-right: zoom controls + minimap navigation.\n2. Connecting FabricJS with React\nFabricJS directly controls the <canvas> element.\nInitialize FabricJS once and store the canvas instance globally.\nTools interact with the shared FabricJS instance.\n3. Tool Architecture\nKeep drawing logic separate from the Canvas component.\nClicking a tool updates global state (activeTool).\nTool components activate based on the selected tool.\nExample: Pen tool enables isDrawingMode and brush settings.\n4. AI Features\nAI tools can analyze and improve the whiteboard. ✨\nExport canvas as JSON using fabricCanvas.toJSON().\nSend board data to AI APIs like Gemini for analysis.\nAI can clean layouts, organize nodes, or suggest architecture improvements.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "DONE ✅\n1. UI/UX Layout Strategy (BoardPage)\nFull-screen whiteboard with clean, distraction-free UI.\nCanvas covers entire screen (100vw × 100vh).\nTop navbar: board name, users, share & export buttons.\nLeft toolbar: pen, shapes, text, sticky notes, eraser.\nRight sidebar: edit properties or open AI tools.\nBottom-right: zoom controls + minimap navigation.\n2. Connecting FabricJS with React\nFabricJS directly controls the <canvas> element.\nInitialize FabricJS once and store the canvas instance globally.\nTools interact with the shared FabricJS instance.\n3. Tool Architecture\nKeep drawing logic separate from the Canvas component.\nClicking a tool updates global state (activeTool).\nTool components activate based on the selected tool.\nExample: Pen tool enables isDrawingMode and brush settings.\n4. AI Features\nAI tools can analyze and improve the whiteboard. ✨\nExport canvas as JSON using fabricCanvas.toJSON().\nSend board data to AI APIs like Gemini for analysis.\nAI can clean layouts, organize nodes, or suggest architecture improvements.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
